      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-101716",
      ":question/problem": "Calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for $y=2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-10x+7{x}^{3}-1.$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Taking the derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-10x+7{x}^{3}-1) \\\\  & =2(\\frac{1}{x})-10+21{x}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{x}-10+21{x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
    },
